LAN-401 — the matching change to scripts/production/**, for Brian to apply.

Agents may not edit anything under `scripts/production/`, and these three
files hold the same vocabulary the migration corrects. Until this diff is
applied, a database built from the baseline still seats `N/T` and `E — End`
and has none of the six additions, and a showcase load would write the old
spellings back.

Apply it from the repository root:

    git apply docs/ux/review/LAN-401/production-scripts.diff

What it does, and why each number is what it is:

  * `scripts/production/baseline/season-2026-27.sql` — `N/T` becomes `NT`,
    `E` is labelled `Edge` rather than `End`, and `DT`, `DE`, `LG`, `RG`,
    `LT` and `RT` are appended at sort_order 18 to 23. Those are exactly the
    values `supabase/migrations/20261001090000_roster_vocabulary_and_warmup.sql`
    computes for this vocabulary (`max(sort_order)` is 17, and the migration
    adds 1 to 6 to it in that order), so a database built fresh from this
    file and a database migrated from the old one are identical. No existing
    code's sort_order moves.

  * `scripts/production/showcase/plan/reference.mjs` — the same six codes in
    the same order, appended to `POSITIONS`, where `sort_order = list index`
    gives them the same 18 to 23. The showcase's position ids are UUIDv5 of
    (vocabulary id, code), so renaming `N/T` to `NT` changes that one id; the
    loader adopts whatever row already carries the code, so on a database the
    migration has already renamed it reconciles onto the existing row rather
    than inserting a second one.

  * `scripts/production/showcase/plan/people.mjs` — the illustrative defence
    assignment list says `NT`, because `N/T` no longer exists to point at.

The showcase seeds no `special_teams_assignments`, no `kit_issue_records`
and, for the same reason, no warmup assignments; the eight warmup small
groups are reference data the migration itself inserts, exactly as the
special-teams squad lists and the kit option lists are. So nothing in
`scripts/production/` has to change for the Warmup assignments group.

`tests/production-baseline-contract.test.ts` counts the baseline's positions
from the baseline file rather than holding the number twice, so it is correct
both before and after this diff is applied.

